---
export const title = 'Ghost text';
export const order = 500;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
import DemoScript from '../../../../components/DemoScript.astro';
---

<p>
  With <code>ai-completion</code> and a provider that offers completions (ADR-030002), a pause in
  typing at the end of a line shows how the assistant would go on, in grey after the caret.
  <strong>Tab</strong> takes it, <strong>Ctrl+→</strong> (<strong>⌘→</strong>) takes the next word,
  and <strong>Escape</strong> or typing dismisses it. Nothing is inserted until the person takes it.
  Type a sentence about the laptop below and pause.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-textarea
    label='Resolution notes'
    ai-completion
    rows='4'
    value='Replaced the screen on LT-0412 and ran the display test.'
    style='max-width: 36rem;'
  ></wc-textarea>
  <script type='module' src='/assets/js/ai-demo.js'></script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<DemoScript name='ai-demo' />

<p>
  The demo uses a scripted provider. An app registers its own once with
  <code>setPeacockAi({'{ provider }'})</code> (see <a href='/ai/'>AI setup</a> for when and where); <code>complete()</code> gets the text before and after
  the caret and an <code>AbortSignal</code> that aborts when the person keeps typing:
</p>

<pre><code>import {'{ setPeacockAi }'} from '@redvars/peacock';

setPeacockAi({'{'}
  provider: {'{'}
    complete: ({'{ before, after, signal, context }'}) =>
      api.complete({'{ before, after, field: context.label }'}, {'{ signal }'}),
  {'}'},
{'}'});</code></pre>

<h3>When it is not offered</h3>
<p>
  Ghost text is opt-in per field, because in short fields it gets in the way. It is never offered
  while the page has AI off, on <code>sensitive</code> fields, or on read-only and disabled fields.
  Only the text of this field is sent.
</p>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  While a suggestion shows, the textarea's description reads "Suggestion: …. Press Tab to accept,
  Escape to dismiss." (the <code>aiGhostHint</code> string). Tab moves focus as usual whenever no
  suggestion shows.
</p>
